# Renders are build outputs. Without this, every one-line model change buries
# the model diff -- the thing peer review is supposed to read -- under eleven
# regenerated files including a binary .docx.
#
# `**/render/**`, not `render/**`. A gitattributes pattern containing a slash is
# anchored to the directory holding this file, so `render/**` matched only a
# top-level `render/` -- which does not exist. Every real render lives under
# `example/render/` or `engagements/<name>/render/`, and neither got the
# attribute: `git check-attr -a example/render/c4-context.svg` printed nothing.
# The control this comment describes had never actually applied.
**/render/** linguist-generated=true

# NOT `-diff` on the whole tree. That marks a file binary, and
# traceability.md, traceability.csv, the .mmd and the .puml are exactly the
# renders a reviewer benefits from reading. Collapse them by default
# (linguist-generated above), but keep them diffable when someone expands one.
# Only the Word document is genuinely unreadable as text.
**/render/*.docx binary
*.docx binary

# A CRLF checkout would not break G6 -- canon.py normalises line endings before
# comparing -- but it would make every render diff noise.
* text=auto eol=lf
